{
  "abstract": "Unconditional Lean 4 + Mathlib formalization for Graham and Harary's hypercube diameter-preserving spanning subgraph problem: proves the universal lower bound 2^n + ceil((2^n - 2n)/(n - 1)) <= f(n) for all n >= 2, raises the asymptotic second-term coefficient to 3/2 on the scale 2^n/(n - 1), and certifies 39 <= f(5) <= 40, f(6) >= 76, f(7) >= 150, f(8) >= 294, and lower bounds for every dimension 17 <= n <= 32. Coverage by this package's Palomar comparison: of the companion paper's 14 main results, 5 are compared in Lean in full (36%; Theorems 1, 3, 9 and 11 and Proposition 13) and 1 in part (Proposition 12: its instances f(6) >= 76 and f(8) >= 294, not its general certificate bridge); 7 more (Corollary 2, Proposition 4, Lemma 5, Theorem 6 and Propositions 7, 8 and 10) are proved in this package's Lean library but not compared; Proposition 14 is outside this comparison (the Lean library rules out valid 19-edge subgraphs of Q_4; its count of 8,320 labelled 20-edge graphs in 30 classes is by external enumeration only); Conjecture 15 is open and not counted. Companion write-up and prior-work search log (including Google Scholar sweep on 2026-11-22) are published at https://mathdiscoveries.org/results/hypercube-edge-bounds; no priority is claimed over unread sources (the full body of Bouabdallah-Delorme-Djelloul 1995 and Djelloul's 1993 thesis could not be accessed).",
